---
layout: base.njk
title: Costs
wide: true
description: "Open operating-cost ledger: cash, forecasts, reserves and noncash time kept separate. Unknown means unknown."
---
<p class="kicker">Open books · Quartermaster ledger 0.1 draft</p>
<h1>What this costs</h1>
<p class="lede">If we can explain how to run it, we should explain what it costs.</p>
<div class="notice">
  <p><strong>{{ costs.summary.statement }}</strong></p>
  <p>As of {{ costs.as_of_utc }}. {{ costs.note }} Source: <a href="{% sourceLink "launch/costs.json" %}"><code>launch/costs.json</code></a>, which <code>qm validate</code> checks on every build (<a href="/costs/ledger.json">machine-readable copy</a>, <a href="/spec/quartermaster/">format</a>).</p>
</div>

{% macro amount(v) %}{% if v === null %}<span class="badge unknown">unknown</span>{% else %}${{ v | round(2) }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

{% for cat, label in costs.categories %}
{% set rows = [] %}{% for e in costs.entries %}{% if e.category == cat %}{% set rows = (rows.push(e), rows) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% if rows.length %}
<h2>{{ label }} <small>(<code>{{ cat }}</code>)</small></h2>
<div class="table-scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Provider</th>{% if cat == "donated-labor" or cat == "user-attention" %}<th scope="col">Hours</th>{% endif %}<th scope="col">Amount ({{ costs.currency }})</th><th scope="col">Date</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for e in rows %}
    <tr><td>{{ e.item }}</td><td>{{ e.provider }}</td>{% if cat == "donated-labor" or cat == "user-attention" %}<td class="num">{% if e.hours === null %}<span class="badge unknown">unmeasured</span>{% else %}{{ e.hours }}{% endif %}</td>{% endif %}<td class="num">{{ amount(e.amount) }}</td><td>{{ e.date or "—" }}{% if e.recurrence %} · {{ e.recurrence }}{% endif %}</td><td>{{ e.status }}</td><td>{{ costs.sourceById[e.source].description }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<h2>Human attention</h2>
<p>No method or hourly rate has been adopted, so time is shown as unmeasured rather than given a price. <a href="/charter/#human-attention">Human Attention Accounting</a> is an open proposal.</p>

<h2>Income, conversions and a treasury</h2>
<p>This ledger covers spending only. JRC has no income, no reserves and no bitcoin. A draft <a href="/treasury/">treasury journal</a> and <a href="{% sourceLink "BITCOIN-TREASURY.md" %}">RFC</a> propose how a project could publish income, conversions and holdings in books nobody can quietly rewrite.</p>

<h2>Propose a saving</h2>
<p>Know a cheaper or sturdier way to run this? Open a pull request using the <a href="{{ repoUrl }}/blob/main/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/propose-a-saving.md">propose-a-saving template</a>, with before-and-after unit costs, your estimate method, the risks, and how we'd measure the result afterwards. Nothing is auto-deployed.</p>


<h2 id="compare">Compare configurations</h2>
<p>Describe two ways of running a project as JSON and compare them. Everything is computed in your browser from the numbers you enter, in whole cents; unknown costs stay unknown. These are estimates, not measurements. The same logic is in the <code>compare_infrastructure_costs</code>, <code>estimate_savings</code> and <code>prepare_cost_reduction_pr</code> agent tools and in <code>qm compare</code> / <code>qm savings</code>. The example below is illustrative; the VPS price is a placeholder, not a quote.</p>
<section data-jrc-compare hidden aria-labelledby="compare-h">
  <h3 id="compare-h" class="visually-hidden">Cost comparison</h3>
  <form class="adopt-form">
    <p><label for="cfg-a">Configuration A (current)</label><br><textarea id="cfg-a" name="a" rows="10" spellcheck="false">{
  "name": "current",
  "currency": "USD",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "hosting",
      "description": "Cloudflare Pages",
      "unit_cost": 0,
      "quantity": 1,
      "period": "monthly",
      "assumption": "Free plan, from launch/costs.json"
    },
    {
      "id": "domain",
      "description": "Domain renewal",
      "unit_cost": 11.2,
      "quantity": 1,
      "period": "yearly",
      "assumption": "Registrar renewal price, from launch/costs.json"
    }
  ]
}</textarea></p>
    <p><label for="cfg-b">Configuration B (proposed)</label><br><textarea id="cfg-b" name="b" rows="10" spellcheck="false">{
  "name": "example-vps",
  "currency": "USD",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "vps",
      "description": "Small virtual server",
      "unit_cost": 5.0,
      "quantity": 1,
      "period": "monthly",
      "assumption": "Illustrative placeholder, not a quote: replace with a real provider's price"
    },
    {
      "id": "domain",
      "description": "Domain renewal",
      "unit_cost": 11.2,
      "quantity": 1,
      "period": "yearly",
      "assumption": "Unchanged"
    },
    {
      "id": "setup",
      "description": "Initial setup",
      "unit_cost": null,
      "quantity": 1,
      "period": "one-time",
      "assumption": "Unknown: depends on who does it"
    }
  ]
}</textarea></p>
    <p><label for="horizon">Horizon (months)</label> <input id="horizon" name="horizon" type="number" min="1" max="120" value="24"></p>
    <p><label for="migration">One-time migration cost (0 if none; leave blank if unknown)</label> <input id="migration" name="migration" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="0"> <label for="migration-assumption">Based on</label> <input id="migration-assumption" name="migration_assumption" type="text" maxlength="300"></p>
    <p><label for="pr-title">PR title (for the PR draft)</label> <input id="pr-title" name="title" type="text" maxlength="100"></p>
    <p><button type="submit" value="compare">Compare</button> <button type="submit" value="savings">Estimate savings</button> <button type="submit" value="pr">Draft a cost-reduction PR</button></p>
  </form>
  <p data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
  <div data-results></div>
</section>
<p data-jrc-nojs>Without JavaScript: save each configuration as JSON and run <code>qm compare A.json B.json</code> or <code>qm savings MODEL.json</code>.</p>
<script type="module" src="/assets/interop.js"></script>
